  "step_2": "The individual in the verbal report compares the monetary difference (100 Euros) between the possible winnings (2500 vs. 2400) with the difference in probability (1%: 34% vs. 33%). The individual states that 'the 2500 Euro win is only one percent less probable' and concludes that they chose the 'marginal higher risk but significantly higher reward' — i.e., Lottery B. The deliberation centers on the relative size of the monetary gain (100 €) versus the small difference in probability (1%). The individual does not mention or consider the least probable outcomes in isolation, nor does the individual compare the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability. Instead, the focus is on the net gain and the probability difference, suggesting a risk-reward trade-off rather than a comparison of the least probable outcomes. Thus, the individual's consideration is based on the magnitude of the gain and the probability difference, not on identifying and comparing the least probable outcomes as defined by the decision reason.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying the least probable outcome (i.e., the outcome with the lowest probability) in each lottery and comparing the monetary value of that outcome. In this case, the least probable outcome is 2500 € in B (33%) and 2400 € in A (34%). Since 33% < 34%, the 2500 € outcome has the lower probability and is thus the 'least probable outcome'. The reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable (higher) value in this least probable outcome — which is 2500 € in B. However, the verbal report does not mention the least probable outcome at all. Instead, the individual compares the 100 € difference in prize with a 1% difference in probability and makes a risk-reward judgment. There is no reference to the least probable outcome or to comparing the monetary value of such outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The justification is based on a different principle (risk-reward trade-off), not on the rule of evaluating the least probable outcome. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
