  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the least probable outcome (i.e., the worst outcome with the lowest probability) and prefer the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., better) such outcome. In this case, the worst outcome is 0 Euro in both lotteries. The probability of this outcome is 80% in A and 75% in B. Since 75% < 80%, the 0 Euro outcome in B occurs with a lower probability, meaning it is less likely to happen — thus, it is more favorable (i.e., less of a risk) in the worst-case scenario. Therefore, according to the decision reason, B should be preferred. However, the individual in the verbal report does not mention the probability of the worst outcome at all. Instead, they focus on the higher prize in A and the fact that the worst case is the same. The individual does not evaluate or compare the probability of the 0 Euro outcome. The justification is based on the value of the prize and the absence of loss, not on the probability of the worst outcome. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information relevant to the reason (the probability of the worst outcome) is not considered. The justification does not reflect the rule of the decision reason (prefer the lottery with the more favorable least probable outcome). Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
